const practicalGuides=[["open-sales-orders","SAP B1 Open Sales Order SQL Query","Find outstanding sales order lines with remaining quantity.","SELECT H.DocNum, H.DocDate, H.CardCode, L.ItemCode, L.Quantity, L.OpenQty FROM ORDR H JOIN RDR1 L ON H.DocEntry=L.DocEntry WHERE H.CANCELED='N' AND H.DocStatus='O' AND L.LineStatus='O' AND L.OpenQty>0 ORDER BY H.DocDate, H.DocNum;","Use OpenQty rather than original Quantity to identify the remaining commitment. A partially delivered order for 10 units with 4 delivered should show 6 open units. Closed lines are excluded."],["open-purchase-orders","SAP B1 Open Purchase Order SQL Query","Identify outstanding purchase order quantities by vendor.","SELECT H.DocNum,H.DocDate,H.CardCode,L.ItemCode,L.Quantity,L.OpenQty FROM OPOR H JOIN POR1 L ON H.DocEntry=L.DocEntry WHERE H.CANCELED='N' AND H.DocStatus='O' AND L.LineStatus='O' AND L.OpenQty>0 ORDER BY H.DocDate,H.DocNum;","An order for 100 units with 60 received has 40 remaining. This measures open purchasing commitments, not unpaid invoices."],["warehouse-stock","SAP B1 Warehouse Stock SQL Query","Report on-hand, committed, ordered and projected inventory.","SELECT W.ItemCode,I.ItemName,W.WhsCode,W.OnHand,W.IsCommited,W.OnOrder,W.OnHand-W.IsCommited+W.OnOrder AS ProjectedQty FROM OITW W JOIN OITM I ON I.ItemCode=W.ItemCode ORDER BY W.ItemCode,W.WhsCode;","For 100 on hand, 30 committed and 20 ordered, projected quantity is 90. Projected quantity includes expected receipts and is not physical stock."],["ap-invoice-balance","SAP B1 Unpaid AP Invoice SQL Query","List open vendor invoices and remaining document balances in local currency.","SELECT DocNum,CardCode,CardName,DocDate,DocDueDate,DocTotal,PaidToDate,DocTotal-PaidToDate AS RemainingLC FROM OPCH WHERE CANCELED='N' AND DocStatus='O' AND DocTotal-PaidToDate>0 ORDER BY DocDueDate;","An invoice of 1000 with 400 applied has a remaining balance of 600. This is a document-level local-currency view, not a complete vendor reconciliation or aging report."],["ar-invoice-balance","SAP B1 Unpaid AR Invoice SQL Query","List open customer invoices and outstanding local-currency balances.","SELECT DocNum,CardCode,CardName,DocDate,DocDueDate,DocTotal,PaidToDate,DocTotal-PaidToDate AS RemainingLC FROM OINV WHERE CANCELED='N' AND DocStatus='O' AND DocTotal-PaidToDate>0 ORDER BY DocDueDate;","An invoice of 5000 with 2000 applied leaves 3000. Review credit memos, installments and internal reconciliation separately for formal aging."],["journal-entry-detail","SAP B1 Journal Entry SQL Query","Retrieve journal entry debit and credit lines with account names.","SELECT H.TransId,H.RefDate,L.Line_ID,L.Account,A.AcctName,L.Debit,L.Credit FROM OJDT H JOIN JDT1 L ON H.TransId=L.TransId LEFT JOIN OACT A ON A.AcctCode=L.Account ORDER BY H.TransId,L.Line_ID;","A journal entry debiting bank 100 and crediting revenue 100 should return two lines. Debit and Credit are local-currency amounts; use appropriate currency fields for foreign currency reporting."]];
